# Entry 3.35: the even-part identities (R2), (R3)

With `T1, T2, T3` the theta series of `x²+xy+12y²`, `2x²+xy+6y²`, `3x²+xy+4y²` (`E35e.lean`):
* `R3`: `T3(q) + T3(−q) = 2(T2(q²) + T3(q²) − T3(q⁴))`,
* `R2`: `T2(q) + T2(−q) = 2(T3(q²) + T1(q²) − T2(q⁴))`.
These are the Hecke relations at the split prime `2`. In `ℂ((t))` (`t² = q`) each is a chain of parity splits
and unimodular changes of variables of the forms (`SR3*`, `SR2*`), and `q ↦ −q` is read off coset by coset: on
`y` even the sign of `Θ3(−q)` is `(−1)^x`, on `y` odd it is `+1` (for `Θ2`: `+1` on `y` even, `(−1)^x` on `y` odd),
so `Θ(−q)` is the sum of the orthogonal theta-product expansions `LRY0m`, `LRY1` (`LRZ0`, `LRZ1m`).
